## 6. What you may always do without permission

These do not require permission and do not count as Rebranding:

- Use the Work inside your own company, on your own projects, for client work.
- Modify it for internal use and never Distribute the modification.
- Teach with it, write about it, or demonstrate it, with attribution.
- Reference it, link to it, or recommend it.
- Fork it to submit a pull request.
- Build websites and applications using it — the sites you build are yours, entirely, with no attribution required on them.

